-- =========================================================================
-- Module + Ref — the first-class module concept (module-substrate Phase 1).
--
-- A `Module` is an entity value carrying a scoped `Name → Ref` view over the
-- one global registry (design/module-system.md "The model"). It is NOT a new
-- primitive — it is the next subsumption in the lineage that turned typeclasses
-- into entity types: the TS `FenelModule` bundle becomes a Fenel `Module` value.
--
--   members : Map String Ref   -- the scoped Name → Ref view (OQ1).
--
-- name / label / description / icon are NOT fields — they ride on
-- Codeable / Labelable / Describable / Iconable instances keyed by the Module
-- INSTANCE's id, exactly like every other entity (the nominal "names are
-- projections keyed by id" pattern — phase-0-inventory § 1.1). Submodule nesting
-- falls out of `members` itself: a member whose Ref points at another Module IS a
-- namespace. No `parent` field needed for the MVP.
--
-- `Ref` is a nominal id pointing at ANY definition (type / function / instance /
-- module). MVP: nominal token over today's id model (OQ2 — codeName strings, no
-- UUID). A Ref spans all definition kinds, so it is deliberately NOT `Id<SomeEntity>`
-- (no phantom). The phantom-breadth — a typed, kind-aware Ref — is exactly what
-- the `typed-function-references` workstream later refines; do not build it here.
--
-- DIVERGENCE (AGENTS.md divergence-documentation rule): the parser has no
-- non-opaque type-alias surface yet (a bare `Ref = Id` parses as a single
-- nullary-constructor variant `{Id}`, not an alias to the `Id` type — see
-- fenel-parser.ts `parseOpaqueDecl` / `opaqueBodyIsTypeExpr`, the alias arm only
-- fires under the `opaque "<repr>"` keyword). So `Ref`'s structural type is
-- registered as `{$ref: "Id"}` via `defineSystemEntity` in system-entities.ts;
-- this file stays the source of truth for the INTENT (Ref ≡ Id). `Module` rounds
-- trips cleanly through `loadFenelModule` (path a) — its parsed `$record` (with the
-- `members : Map String Ref` `$map` field) is used as-is. The bare-alias syntax is
-- the parser's Phase 2.12 follow-up, out of scope for this additive phase.
-- =========================================================================

Ref = Id

-- FM-retire-E1 Step 7 — `Module`'s catalog identity rides on these directives
-- (loader-lifted to Codeable / Labelable / Describable / Iconable, auto-
-- registered by system-entities.ts via the moduleCore facet-threading). Its
-- inline `defineSystemEntity` is DELETED. `Ref` (above) carries NO directive —
-- it stays inert (no lifted Codeable → the auto-loop's gate skips it); its flip
-- waits on the bare type-alias surface (D1, typed-function-references Tier 3).
@entity
@label "Module"
@icon "box"
@description "A scoped Name → Ref view over the one global registry — Fenel's first-class module value (design/module-system.md). `members : Map String Ref` is the scope; a member whose Ref points at another Module is a submodule (namespace, for free). The next subsumption in the lineage that turned typeclasses into entity types: the TS `FenelModule` bundle becomes a Fenel `Module` value."
Module = Module members: Map String Ref
